---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Sports Psychology Degree: Programs, Careers and Salary"
  description="Explore sports psychology degree programs: bachelor's, master's, and PhD options, admission requirements, costs, careers, and salary outlook in the US."
  ogImage="/images/training-plan-equipment.webp"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Degrees</p>
      <h1>Sports Psychology Degrees</h1>
      <p>From bachelor's to master's and PhD programs, compare degree levels, online options, and certification paths in sports psychology.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="page-body">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p>A sports psychology degree prepares you to help athletes perform at their best. Most professional roles require a master's degree or higher, with doctoral programs opening doors to licensed practice, research, and university teaching. Online programs have made graduate study more accessible for working professionals.</p>
      <p>Our full guides will compare program types, accreditation, admission requirements, and costs, so you can choose the path that fits your goals. Pair this with our <a href="/careers/">careers guide</a> to see where each degree level can take you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
